{
  "case_id": "2020-20-437",
  "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The text of Section 1326(d) resolves the question presented in this case. In a provision entitled \"Limitation on Collateral Attacks on Underlying Deportation Order,\" Congress stated that a non-citizen may not challenge the validity of his removal order unless he demonstrates that he exhausted any available administrative remedies, that the removal proceedings improperly deprived him of the right to judicial review, and that the entry of the order was fundamentally unfair."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument next in Case 20-437, United States versus Palomar-Santiago."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent plainly could have brought to the BIA, the court of appeals, and, if necessary, this Court the argument that his prior offense was not an aggravated felony, just as others later did."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Counsel, I want to make sure I understand the government's position correctly. Are -- are there any removal orders that are subject to collateral attack if the alien cannot establish the three requirements of subsection (d)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Ms. Ross, I'd like to talk about this word \"available\" and give you a hypothetical. Suppose that the immigration judge in this case had told the alien, you know, there -- there just isn't an administrative procedure that you can take my ruling to, this is it, this is the end of the line. What would happen in that case? Would -- would -- would -- would this provision be satisfied?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So how is that distinguishable from this case? Because, in this case, there's just as much an error in the first -- from the IJ."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1326(d)'s text is clear and it resolves the question presented in this case. The immigration judge's determination that Respondent's prior offense qualified as an aggravated felony does not demonstrate, as Congress required Respondent to do, that he exhausted any available administrative remedies or that the removal proceedings improperly deprived him of the opportunity for judicial review."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Bradley N. Garcia",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This indictment was properly dismissed for two reasons. First, a Section 1326 prosecution cannot proceed based on an invalid removal order. And this case can be resolved on the narrow ground that the invalidity of the order here is undisputed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, are you -- is it your argument that the administrative remedies are so complicated that they would always be unavailable?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Bradley N. Garcia",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It would be extremely anomalous to think that Congress wanted to impose this particular criminal punishment when everybody agrees that the order was invalid."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How, in your opinion, at the risk of repetition, do you get out of this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose that Leocal and the Ninth Circuit decision, Trinidad -- Trinidad Aquino, had not been decided, but everything else about this case is the same. Could your client have moved to dismiss the indictment in this case on the grounds that the prior removal order was invalid for the reasons that were later -- later accepted and that would later be accepted in Leocal and -- and the Ninth Circuit decision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you accept the validity of the deportation order?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0001-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Garcia, assuming we are in Section 1326(d) and the question is one of availability, I had understood your brief to be making the argument that this is essentially a misrepresentation case, as described in Ross, so that even if there was an administrative remedy on the books, it wasn't truly available."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Plainly, there was a misrepresentation, willful or not, and that combines with the fact that this area, the categorical approach, is already so opaque, as the Court put it in Ross, so confusing, no reasonable prisoner, here, a non-citizen, can use them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Mr. Garcia, I'd like to go back to the colloquy you were just having with Justice Kagan. So I take you to be saying that, and I think everybody, I was about to say, in this room, but on this call, can sympathize with your point that the categorical approach can be opaque and confusing, but does that then mean that availability under 1326(d) varies according to the difficulty of the law that underlay the initial conviction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: A minute to wrap up, Mr. Garcia."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-20-437",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "443db17cf31b1df30f013ad8aaeab15f42366d4d44b9c24df3c0fec2d4a784a8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-443db17cf31b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "argument today, his invalidity argument, is entirely circular."
    },
